  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Approximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.1060$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.3\\,$ | $\\,0.0901\\,$ | $\\,0.0885\\,$ | $\\,0.0869\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.2\\,$ | $\\,0.1075\\,$ | $\\,0.1056\\,$ | $\\,0.1038\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.1271\\,$ | $\\,0.1251\\,$ | $\\,0.1230\\,$ |",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.1060$ lies between. These numbers are $0.1056$ and $0.1075.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.1056 & <0.1060<0.1075\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $\u03a6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(-1.25) & <\u03a6(z)<\u03a6(-1.24).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz\u2248\\frac{-1.25+(-1.24)}{2}=-1.245.\n$$",
